---
title: Tina's Bars
author: Aunt Vera McFall
category: Cookies
cook time: 25 minutes
source: Loving Memories of Mildred
---

@shortening{0.5%cup}
@egg{1}
@vanilla{1%tsp}
@baking soda{0.5%tsp}
@walnuts{0.5%cup}
@brown sugar{1%cup}
@oatmeal{2%cups}
@salt{0.5%tsp}
@flour{0.75%cup}
@chocolate chips{1%12-oz package}
@condensed milk{1%can}
@salt{0.25%tsp}

Combine shortening, egg, vanilla, baking soda, walnuts, brown sugar, oatmeal, 1/2 tsp salt, and flour. Press 2/3 of mixture into 9x13 pan. Combine and melt (very low heat) 12-oz package of chocolate chips. Add 1 can condensed milk and 1/4 tsp salt. Spread on first mixture. Add remaining dough (just drop on in splotches). Bake at 350 degrees for 25 minutes. Cut into squares.
